    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>AKS pod identity gives pods running in Kubernetes their own first-class identity in Azure Active Directory. Pods can now securely communicate with Azure services like Key Vault or Storage without having to manage their own secrets or worry about rotating keys.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fazure.microsoft.com%2Fen-us%2Fservices%2Fkubernetes-service%2F&amp;data=02%7C01%7Cv-krwea%40microsoft.com%7C4ea920cae8ac4851a74308d68544d1bc%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C636842927955229218&amp;sdata=tnh9LTP5h%2B5O8B0umDDekbOtmT3D1neYxNgEl0M6wi8%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more about AKS.</a></p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "AKS pod identity gives pods running in Kubernetes their own first-class identity in Azure Active Directory. Pods can now securely communicate with Azure services like Key Vault or Storage without having to manage their own secrets or worry about rotating keys.\n\nLearn more about AKS."
